{"type":"text","timestamp":1794339486911,"sessionID":"ses_e390f5f67ffeyzZwSqPLXNKUwZ","part":{"id":"prt_1c6f7bcaa001UtqUtn0rJhS5f4","messageID":"msg_1c6f7aa15001Z9Jz0zOTDCP411","sessionID":"ses_e390f5f67ffeyzZwSqPLXNKUwZ","type":"text","text":"<think>Now let me test the backend. Let me install the backend deps in a venv and run the app.\n\nActually, let me create a virtualenv at /workspace/.venv (gitignored? .dockerignore ignores .venv ✓). Let me check .gitignore — there is none. Hmm, the repo has no .gitignore. The .dockerignore excludes node_modules, .venv, data/*.db. But git would track .venv if I create it in the workspace. Let me create the venv outside the workspace... but external directories are restricted (only /tmp/opencode allowed? The earlier denial was for /tmp/opencode which is supposedly pre-approved but the rule \"external_directory pattern * deny\" blocked it).\n\nHmm, the earlier error said the rule prevents using that tool call with the pattern list including \"external_directory\": {\"pattern\": \"/tmp/opencode/*\", \"action\": \"allow\"} and {\"pattern\": \"*\", \"action\": \"deny\"}. The deny rule with pattern * might have matched first. Let me try creating a venv in /workspace/.venv and add a .gitignore entry. The .dockerignore already excludes .venv from the Docker context, so the image build is unaffected. For git, I'll add a .gitignore file (that's a reasonable addition, not a doc file).\n\nActually, is installing into the system python OK? `pip install flask gunicorn` globally — the sandbox may allow it (pip download worked). Installing globally is simpler and avoids polluting the repo. But it modifies the system... it's a sandbox, fine. Actually, using a venv inside /workspace/.venv plus a .gitignore is cleaner and standard.\n\nLet me do: python3 -m venv /workspace/.venv && .venv/bin/pip install -r backend/requirements.txt.\n\nWait — but will the venv include the `data` dir? The app writes to ./data relative to CWD. I'll run from /workspace so the data dir is /workspace/data. That's fine (gitignored via .gitignore).\n\nLet me setit up.</think>\n\n","time":{"start":1794339486890,"end":1794339486907}}}
