{"type":"text","timestamp":1794339691155,"sessionID":"ses_e390f5f67ffeyzZwSqPLXNKUwZ","part":{"id":"prt_1c6fada6900143rWR7KZIRtyys","messageID":"msg_1c6faceb9001hh6Y3tlVruetI6","sessionID":"ses_e390f5f67ffeyzZwSqPLXNKUwZ","type":"text","text":"<think>The background process gets killed when the shell command finishes/times out. The bash tool seems to kill the process group on timeout.\n\nLet me try a different approach: run the server and the test in the SAME bash command, so the server lives during the test.\n\nE.g.:\n```bash\ncd /workspace && rm -rf data && ADMIN_PASSWORD=admin-pw .venv/bin/gunicorn --bind 127.0.0.1:8000 --pythonpath backend app:app > /tmp/gunicorn.log 2>&1 &\nSRV=$!\nsleep 3\n.venv/bin/python scripts/check_api.py\nkill $SRV\n```\n\nThat should work within one command.</think>\n\n","time":{"start":1794339691113,"end":1794339691151}}}
