{"type":"text","timestamp":1794339917066,"sessionID":"ses_e390f5f67ffeyzZwSqPLXNKUwZ","part":{"id":"prt_1c6fe4cf8001vlxqZa0jdzFCJr","messageID":"msg_1c6fe3f62001Oc6DnfCZwKl300","sessionID":"ses_e390f5f67ffeyzZwSqPLXNKUwZ","type":"text","text":"<think>Wait, there's an issue with the `ensure_admin_account` call: it's only triggered when the username is \"admin\" and no account row exists. But `username.casefold() == ADMIN_USERNAME` — the admin account is stored as \"admin\" and the lookup is case-insensitive (COLLATE NOCASE) ✓.\n\nHmm, but there's a subtlety: `ensure_admin_account` inserts the admin with `login_enabled=1` only if ADMIN_PASSWORD is set ✓.\n\nNow, another thought about the rate-limit check and the account-not-found case: I record the client attempt for unknown usernames ✓ (so they count toward the limit).\n\nNow let me re-run the tests. Note the test script's rate-limit check expects the first 20 attempts → 401 and the 21st → 429 ✓ (unknown usernames → recorded).\n\nLet me re-run the test suite.</think>\n\n","time":{"start":1794339917048,"end":1794339917062}}}
