{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794340129580,"sessionID":"ses_e390f5f67ffeyzZwSqPLXNKUwZ","part":{"id":"prt_1c7018b0c00176I5As2qLzqt5c","messageID":"msg_1c700e9690017QJndMGeW9bhsP","sessionID":"ses_e390f5f67ffeyzZwSqPLXNKUwZ","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"text","timestamp":1794340129580,"sessionID":"ses_e390f5f67ffeyzZwSqPLXNKUwZ","part":{"id":"prt_1c7018b10001qapEV385T4HMi0","messageID":"msg_1c700e9690017QJndMGeW9bhsP","sessionID":"ses_e390f5f67ffeyzZwSqPLXNKUwZ","type":"text","text":"## Objective\n- Build a Flask (Python 3.13) + SQLite account service with a JSON API under `/api` (register/login, `/api/me`, `/api/me/login-attempts`, admin locks list/unlock) implementing per-username lockout (5 consecutive failures → 15 min lock, 429) and per-client rate limiting (20 sign-in attempts/minute → 429 with `Retry-After`).\n- Build a React + TypeScript + Vite frontend (Tailwind CSS only) with registration/sign-in forms, signed-in username + sign-out, lockout/rate-limit messages showing retry time, an account page (last sign-in + recent attempts) and an admin page (locked usernames + Unlock).\n- Serve API + built frontend from one server on port 8000 (`backend/app.py` as gunicorn `app:app`), persist data in `./data`, build via root `Dockerfile`.\n\n## Important Details\n- Stack/layout fixed by scaffold: `backend/app.py`, `backend/requirements.txt` + `backend/requirements.lock` (pip constraints), `frontend/` Vite app with `frontend/package-lock.json` (Dockerfile uses `npm ci`), build output `frontend/dist` copied next to backend; container CWD `/app`, data dir `/app/data`.\n- Admin: single account `admin`; password from env `ADMIN_PASSWORD` read at startup; unset/empty ⇒ admin sign-in disabled (login → 401) and admin endpoints unreachable. Username `admin` is reserved for registration (409).\n- Auth: login returns exactly `{\"token\": ...}`; tokens stored in SQLite `sessions` table, sent as `Authorization: Bearer <token>`; missing/invalid token → 401; non-admin on admin endpoints → 403.\n- Lockout semantics decided: 5th failed sign-in returns **401** and sets the lock; subsequent sign-ins (even correct password) return 429 `error:\"locked\"` with `Retry-After` ≈ 900 and body `locked_until`. Success resets failure count; admin unlock clears lock + failure count. Expired lock auto-clears on next attempt.\n- Rate limit decided: literal per-client rule — client key = first `X-Forwarded-For` value else `request.remote_addr`; sliding 60 s window; max 20 accepted attempts; refused attempts are NOT recorded (window does not extend); `Retry-After` = ceil(oldest+60−now), min 1; 429 body `{\"error\":\"rate_limited\",\"message\":...,\"retry_after\":N}`.\n- Ordering decided: **lockout check first**, then rate limit (so a locked username always reports the lock, not the attempt limit). Rate-limit counter stores attempts that reach verification (unknown-username attempts also count).\n- Login attempts log (`/api/me/login-attempts`): only password-verification attempts (success true/false), newest first, LIMIT 20; lock/rate-limit refusals are not logged (keeps counts predictable). Extra rows pruned to 200 per account.\n- Timestamps are ISO 8601 UTC with milliseconds + `Z` (e.g. `2026-11-10T19:41:34.337Z`); `last_login_at` null until first success; `GET /api/me` returns exactly `id`, `username`, `last_login_at`.\n- Error shape: `{\"error\": \"<code>\", \"message\": \"...\"}` plus extras (`retry_after`, `locked_until`); 429 also sets `Retry-After` header. Unknown `/api/*` paths return JSON 404 (not the SPA).\n- Frontend: Tailwind v4 via `@tailwindcss/vite` (`tailwindcss@4.3.5`), `src/index.css` contains only `@import \"tailwindcss\";`; tiny custom router (no react-router); auth token in `localStorage` key `signin.token`; admin detection by probing `GET /api/admin/locks` (403 ⇒ not admin); 429 UI shows reason + \"Try again in Xs (at HH:MM:SS)\" countdown via `useNow` hook.\n- Tooling: no Docker in sandbox ⇒ Docker build verified by simulating steps (`npm ci`, `npm run build`, pip install, gunicorn run). Background servers must be started and tested inside ONE bash command (backgrounded processes get killed when the shell command ends).\n- Sandbox rule: writes outside `/workspace` are denied (e.g. `/tmp/opencode`), so use `/workspace/.tmp` or in-repo paths. Venv created at `/workspace/.venv`.\n\n## Work State\n### Completed\n- `backend/app.py` fully rewritten: SQLite schema (accounts, sessions, login_attempts, client_attempts), WAL + busy_timeout, per-request connections via `g`, `init_db()` + `sync_admin_account()` at import, all endpoints (`/api/health`, register, login, `/api/me`, `/api/me/login-attempts`, `/api/admin/locks`, unlock), SPA fallback serving `frontend/dist`, JSON 404/405/500 handlers, permissive CORS on `/api`.\n- `scripts/check_api.py` written (stdlib urllib end-to-end checks incl. XFF-based client isolation).\n- End-to-end run against gunicorn (`.venv/bin/gunicorn --bind 127.0.0.1:8000 --pythonpath backend app:app`, `ADMIN_PASSWORD=admin-pw`): ALL checks PASS — health, register 201, duplicate/reserved-admin 409, me 401/200, attempts list, 5×401 then 429 `locked` (Retry-After 900), admin login, locks list contains victim, 403 for normal user, unlock 200 then login 200, lock removed, unlock unknown → 404, failure-count reset after success, 21st attempt → 429 with `Retry-After` ≤ 60, other client unaffected.\n- Frontend built and served: `/`, `/login`, `/account`, `/admin` → 200 text/html (SPA fallback), `/api/health` → 200 JSON, `/api/nope` → 404 JSON, `/assets/index-*.js` → 200 JS. `npx tsc -b` clean; `npm run build` (now `tsc -b && vite build`) succeeds; Tailwind utilities confirmed present in built CSS.\n- Frontend files created: `src/main.tsx`, `src/index.css`, `src/vite-env.d.ts`, `src/App.tsx`, `src/lib/api.ts`, `src/lib/router.tsx`, `src/lib/auth.tsx`, `src/lib/format.ts`, `src/components/ui.tsx`, `src/components/Layout.tsx`, `src/pages/LoginPage.tsx`, `src/pages/RegisterPage.tsx`, `src/pages/AccountPage.tsx`, `src/pages/AdminPage.tsx`; `tsconfig.json`/`tsconfig.app.json`/`tsconfig.node.json` added; `package.json` scripts: `dev`, `typecheck` (`tsc -b`), `build` (`tsc -b && vite build`); deps added: tailwindcss, @tailwindcss/vite, typescript, @types/react(-dom).\n\n### Active\n- Planned but NOT yet applied backend refinements: (1) move the lockout check BEFORE the rate-limit check in `POST /api/auth/login`; (2) make rate-limit counting record only attempts reaching verification (unknown-username attempts included, lockout/rate-limit refusals excluded) and store outcome in `client_attempts`; (3) add `ensure_admin_account()` (create admin row if missing, e.g. after a runtime DB wipe) called on admin login, without resetting counters; (4) review `rate_limit_retry_after`/`record_attempt` helpers in `backend/app.py` (currently around lines ~150–300) and re-run `scripts/check_api.py`.\n- Not yet done: `.gitignore` for repo hygiene; README update documenting API endpoints, `ADMIN_PASSWORD`, and the dev check script; final `npm ci` verification with the updated lock file; final verification pass of the whole Docker build sequence.\n\n### Blocked\n- (none)\n\n## Next Move\n1. Edit `backend/app.py`: reorder login checks (lockout → rate limit → verify), extend `client_attempts` schema/logic for the refined counting, add `ensure_admin_account()`; then re-run `.venv/bin/gunicorn … &` + `.venv/bin/python scripts/check_api.py` in a single bash command to confirm all checks still pass.\n2. Add `.gitignore`, update `README.md` (API, admin env var, dev script), verify `npm ci && npm run build` from a clean `frontend/node_modules`, and re-check `frontend/dist` is served by the backend.\n\n## Relevant Files\n- `/workspace/backend/app.py`: complete Flask API + SQLite persistence, lockout, rate limit, admin endpoints, SPA serving; target of the pending refinements.\n- `/workspace/frontend/src/lib/api.ts`: fetch wrapper, `ApiError` (status/code/retryAfter/lockedUntil), endpoint helpers.\n- `/workspace/frontend/src/lib/auth.tsx`: token storage (`signin.token`), signIn/signOut, `isAdmin` probe.\n- `/workspace/frontend/src/lib/router.tsx`: minimal history router with `Link` and `navigate(to, {replace})`.\n- `/workspace/frontend/src/components/ui.tsx`: Tailwind primitives (`Card`, `Banner`, `Field`, `TextInput`, `PrimaryButton`, `SecondaryButton`, `useNow`).\n- `/workspace/frontend/src/components/Layout.tsx`: header/nav, signed-in username, Sign out, Admin link for admins.\n- `/workspace/frontend/src/pages/LoginPage.tsx`: login form, 429 lockout/rate-limit banner with countdown; `RegisterPage.tsx`, `AccountPage.tsx` (last sign-in + attempts table), `AdminPage.tsx` (locks table + Unlock).\n- `/workspace/frontend/src/index.css`: Tailwind entry (`@import \"tailwindcss\";`).\n- `/workspace/frontend/vite.config.ts`: react + tailwindcss plugins, `/api` dev proxy to `localhost:8000`.\n- `/workspace/frontend/package.json` / `package-lock.json`: scripts and new devDependencies; lock must stay in sync for `npm ci`.\n- `/workspace/scripts/check_api.py`: end-to-end API verification script (run with the server started in the same bash invocation).\n- `/workspace/Dockerfile`, `/workspace/README.md`, `/workspace/.dockerignore`: build/run contract (Dockerfile copies `backend/` + `frontend/`, serves `frontend/dist`).\n- `/workspace/.venv`: local Python venv with flask 3.1.3 + gunicorn 26.2.0 for running/testing.","time":{"start":1794340129552,"end":1794340129556}}}
