{"type":"text","timestamp":1794340165997,"sessionID":"ses_e390f5f67ffeyzZwSqPLXNKUwZ","part":{"id":"prt_1c70219610017MtXCBlaW3LW5W","messageID":"msg_1c701c9bf001LL1Y1NKSgNhNZy","sessionID":"ses_e390f5f67ffeyzZwSqPLXNKUwZ","type":"text","text":"<think>All pass. Now let me add the restart persistence and admin-disabled tests as a separate script (they need server restarts), e.g. `scripts/check_restart.py` or extend `run_checks.sh`.\n\nLet me write a shell script that:\n1. Starts the server with ADMIN_PASSWORD=admin-pw, registers a user, logs in, stops the server.\n2. Restarts the server (same data dir), checks /api/me still works with the old token and the user can log in again.\n3. Starts the server WITHOUT ADMIN_PASSWORD → admin login returns 401, /api/admin/locks returns 401 (no token) and admin can't sign in.\n\nLet me implement this as `scripts/check_persistence.sh`.\n\nNote: when ADMIN_PASSWORD is unset, `sync_admin_account` sets the admin password to a random one and login_enabled=0 → the admin login returns 401 ✓.\n\nWait — careful: with `login_enabled=0` for admin, the login path returns 401 invalid_credentials ✓ (admin sign-in disabled).\n\nBut hmm: `ensure_admin_account()` when the admin row is missing and ADMIN_PASSWORD is unset → creates with login_enabled=0 ✓.\n\nLet me write the script.</think>\n\n","time":{"start":1794340165985,"end":1794340165994}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794340166028,"sessionID":"ses_e390f5f67ffeyzZwSqPLXNKUwZ","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"write","callID":"call-9dacf49f-6a84-438f-951c-3fd9a2528aa1","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"#!/usr/bin/env bash\n# Verify that data survives a restart and that admin sign-in is disabled\n# when ADMIN_PASSWORD is not set.\nset -u\ncd /workspace\npkill -f \"[g]unicorn\" >/dev/null 2>&1\nsleep 1\nrm -rf data\n\nFAILED=0\nstart() {\n  .venv/bin/gunicorn --bind 127.0.0.1:8000 --pythonpath backend app:app > /tmp/gunicorn-persist.log 2>&1 &\n  SRV=$!\n  sleep 3\n}\nstop() {\n  kill $SRV >/dev/null 2>&1\n  wait $SRV 2>/dev/null\n}\n\necho \"== first start ==\"\nstart\n.venv/bin/python - <<'PY'\nimport json, urllib.request, urllib.error\n\ndef call(method, path, payload=None, token=None):\n    req = urllib.request.Request(\n        f\"http://127.0.0.1:8000{path}\",\n        method=method,\n        data=json.dumps(payload).encode() if payload is not None else None,\n        headers={\"Content-Type\": \"application/json\"},\n    )\n    if token:\n        req.add_header(\"Authorization\", f\"Bearer {token}\")\n    try:\n        with urllib.request.urlopen(req) as resp:\n            return resp.status, json.loads(resp.read() or b\"{}\")\n    except urllib.error.HTTPError as e:\n        return e.code, json.loads(e.read() or b\"{}\")\n\nstatus, _ = call(\"POST\", \"/api/auth/register\", {\"username\": \"persisted\", \"password\": \"pw\"})\nassert status == 201, status\nstatus, body = call(\"POST\", \"/api/auth/login\", {\"username\": \"persisted\", \"password\": \"pw\"})\nassert status == 200, status\nwith open(\"/workspace/.tmp-token\", \"w\") as fh:\n    fh.write(body[\"token\"])\nprint(\"registered and signed in\")\nPY\nstop\n\necho \"== restart with the same data directory ==\"\nstart\nTOKEN=$(cat /workspace/.tmp-token)\n.venv/bin/python - \"$TOKEN\" <<'PY'\nimport json, sys, urllib.request, urllib.error\n\ntoken = sys.argv[1]\n\ndef call(method, path, payload=None):\n    req = urllib.request.Request(\n        f\"http://127.0.0.1:8000{path}\",\n        method=method,\n        data=json.dumps(payload).encode() if payload is not None else None,\n        headers={\"Content-Type\": \"application/json\", \"Authorization\": f\"Bearer {token}\"},\n    )\n    try:\n        with urllib.request.urlopen(req) as resp:\n            return resp.status, json.loads(resp.read() or b\"{}\")\n    except urllib.error.HTTPError as e:\n        return e.code, json.loads(e.read() or b\"{}\")\n\nstatus, body = call(\"GET\", \"/api/me\")\nassert status == 200 and body[\"username\"] == \"persisted\", (status, body)\nprint(\"session and account survived the restart\")\nPY\nstop\nrm -f /workspace/.tmp-token\n\necho \"== restart without ADMIN_PASSWORD ==\"\nunset ADMIN_PASSWORD\nstart\n.venv/bin/python - <<'PY'\nimport json, urllib.request, urllib.error\n\ndef call(method, path, payload=None):\n    req = urllib.request.Request(\n        f\"http://127.0.0.1:8000{path}\",\n        method=method,\n        data=json.dumps(payload).encode() if payload is not None else None,\n        headers={\"Content-Type\": \"application/json\"},\n    )\n    try:\n        with urllib.request.urlopen(req) as resp:\n            return resp.status, json.loads(resp.read() or b\"{}\")\n    except urllib.error.HTTPError as e:\n        return e.code, json.loads(e.read() or b\"{}\")\n\nstatus, body = call(\"POST\", \"/api/auth/login\", {\"username\": \"admin\", \"password\": \"admin-pw\"})\nassert status == 401, (status, body)\nstatus, body = call(\"POST\", \"/api/auth/login\", {\"username\": \"persisted\", \"password\": \"pw\"})\nassert status == 200, (status, body)\nprint(\"admin sign-in disabled without ADMIN_PASSWORD\")\nPY\nstop\n\necho \"persistence checks passed\"\n","filePath":"/workspace/scripts/check_persistence.sh"},"output":"Wrote file successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"filepath":"/workspace/scripts/check_persistence.sh","exists":false,"truncated":false},"title":"scripts/check_persistence.sh","time":{"start":1794340165991,"end":1794340166010}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[]}},"id":"prt_1c7021963001kkC3NGQXrcYsej","sessionID":"ses_e390f5f67ffeyzZwSqPLXNKUwZ","messageID":"msg_1c701c9bf001LL1Y1NKSgNhNZy"}}
