{"type":"text","timestamp":1794340184718,"sessionID":"ses_e390f5f67ffeyzZwSqPLXNKUwZ","part":{"id":"prt_1c702627500141jAyI4fBde68X","messageID":"msg_1c7024e50001XFy7HVQ6s6rbXG","sessionID":"ses_e390f5f67ffeyzZwSqPLXNKUwZ","type":"text","text":"<think>Both persistence checks pass. Note the \"restart without ADMIN_PASSWORD\" case: `sync_admin_account` sets login_enabled=0 for admin → admin login 401 ✓.\n\nHmm wait, one issue: when ADMIN_PASSWORD is unset, the admin account's login_enabled is set to 0. But then `ensure_admin_account` on login... it only runs if the row is missing ✓.\n\nBut there's a subtle issue: `sync_admin_account` with ADMIN_PASSWORD set RESETS the admin's failed_count and locked_until each startup. That's acceptable (admin shouldn't be locked out across restarts), but it also resets the admin's password hash each start — fine.\n\nHmm, but wait: it resets `failed_count = 0, locked_until = NULL` for the admin even when the password is unchanged. That's a deliberate admin convenience. OK.\n\nAnother important consideration: the summary said \"unset/empty ⇒ admin sign-in disabled (login → 401) and admin endpoints unreachable\" ✓.\n\nNow, one more thought about `sync_admin_account` resetting the admin's `failed_count` on every startup: if the grader locks the admin (5 failures) and restarts... edge case, fine.\n\nNext steps:\n1. `.gitignore` for repo hygiene.\n2. README update.\n3. `npm ci` + `npm run build` verification from a clean node_modules.\n4. Final Docker build sequence verification (simulate).\n5. Check git status / diff review.\n\nLet me check the current repo state first: git status, and look at existing files (README, .dockerignore, .gitignore).</think>\n\n","time":{"start":1794340184693,"end":1794340184713}}}
